  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 133 AM CDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nThe Long Term forecast remains on track. In other words, \"hot and \ngenerally dry\" remains the dominant message through the forecast \nperiod. West Texas and southeast New Mexico still look to stay on \nthe eastern/southeastern periphery of an upper-level ridge centered \nnear or just west of the Four Corners area. As a result, highs \nacross the area remain in the mid-to-upper 90s into next week, with \n100 degree temperatures confined mainly to the river valleys. Lows \nsettle in the mid 70s for most locations every night (60s in usual \ncool spots). Much of the area is still expected to stay dry through \nthe period. However, low (generally 10-30%) shower and thunderstorm \nchances are maintained in and around the higher terrain (mainly in \nthe Davis Mountains) thanks to upsloping winds and weak disturbances \nrounding the edge of the ridge.\n\nSprang",
